L1_1.mode = "text"
L1_1.title = "The Shore"
L1_1.author = "Unknown Author"
L1_1.text = "The sea spat me out. I remember only the water above my head, the salt in my lungs, and then the sand beneath my hands. I was not alone. There were other bodies scattered along the shore. All of them breathing. All of them trembling. None of them remembered how they had arrived here. I remember only something moving beneath the surface. Something enormous. <<PAGE>> [ THE SHADOW ] We saw it at sunset. Or perhaps we saw only a part of it. Too large to be a whale. Too silent to be a storm. A boat tried to leave the island. For a few moments, we thought they had made it. Then the sea rose beneath them. I saw no teeth. I saw no blood. Only the sound of wood breaking, screams swallowed by the water and then... darkness. I woke once again on the same beach. Alive. I do not know whether that thing saved me or simply forced me back. But since that day, I have stopped thinking of the sea as a way out. <<PAGE>> [ ETERIS ] We are no longer hungry. At least not in the way we remember. The body does not ask for bread, meat, or water. It asks only for that blue drink we learned to distill from bitter herbs and treated hides. We call it Eteris. We do not know why it works. We only know what happens when it is gone. The veins turn dark. The skin tightens over the bones. The eyes change. One of us decided to stop drinking it. He said he would rather die than depend on something he did not understand. But he did not die. He still breathes. He still walks. I just do not think he is one of us anymore. And that frightens me more than anything else."
