L1_1.mode = "text"
L1_1.title = "Against the Beast"
L1_1.author = "Order of the Keepers"
L1_1.text = "Brothers of the islands, do not be deceived by the words of those who have forgotten what we once were. The creature that dwells in the sea is not a guardian. It does not protect us. It did not choose us. It is the cause of our ruin. Since it emerged, the waters have devoured the land, entire coastlines have vanished, and our children have begun to be born different. Some call all of this change. Others dare to call it evolution. We remember its true name: Decay. There is no mercy in a boat being shattered before it can reach the horizon. There is no protection in a sea that prevents us from escaping. It is domination. The Sons believe that what we are becoming is the beginning of something new. We know it is the end of what we once were. Eteris slows the corruption. Eteris preserves what remains of man. As long as we have it, we will resist. Do not listen to those who urge you to embrace Decay. Do not follow those who seek answers beyond the sea. Defend the islands. Protect the Eteris. And above all, do not seek the horizon. Some prisons have no need for walls."
