L1_1.title = "Of the Dragon That Was Not Yet a Monster"
L1_1.author = "Ancient Manuscript"
L1_1.text = "Long before the Flooding, when the sea still had known boundaries, fishermen told stories of a rare creature that followed their vessels. They called it a sea dragon, though it was little larger than a man. It did not attack. It did not seem to fear the boats. It would swim alongside their hulls for miles before disappearing into the depths. Some fishermen even began to consider its presence a sign of good fortune. Then something changed. Blue liquids were poured into the currents, and fine ash began to settle upon the water. No one ever discovered where they came from. The little dragon continued to follow the boats. It continued to feed in those same waters, consuming things it could not understand. The fishermen were the first to notice. Beneath its scales appeared glowing veins, blue as the sea beneath a storm. Then the creature vanished. For years, no one saw it again. Much later, something immeasurably larger began to move beneath the waves. Those who remembered the little dragon always refused to call it a coincidence. One of the last fishermen who had seen it wrote only these words: \"It had grown. It had changed. But I recognized its eyes. And in its eyes, it recognized me.\""
