L1_1 = {}
L1_1.mode = "text"
L1_1.title = "Why We Fight"
L1_1.author = "Arena Master"
L1_1.text = "We do not fight for glory. We do not fight out of hatred. And we do not fight because we enjoy seeing blood spilled upon the sand, no matter what those who have never held a weapon may say. We fight because the sea never sleeps. The forests change, the waters drag creatures onto our shores that did not exist yesterday, and the nights are never truly silent. Every man who lives long enough on these islands learns that sooner or later, something will come looking for him. When that moment comes, there is no time to learn. That is why the Arena exists. It is not spectacle. It is preparation. Every scar is a memory. Every blow endured is a lesson paid for with blood instead of life. Here, you can make mistakes. Here, you can fall. Here, someone can drag you from the sand, pour Eteris down your throat, and tell you what you did wrong. Outside the Circle, no one will do that for you. A creature will not stay its claws because you forgot how to defend yourself. The sea will show no mercy because you are tired. Those who fall in the Arena learn not to fall when it truly matters. Remember this when you hear someone call fighting barbaric. Remember it when you see men spitting blood onto the sand while others shout their names. And above all, remember this: those who refuse to fight can do so only because someone else has chosen to fight in their place. Fighting reminds us that we are still here. The old world is gone. We are not. And as long as someone has the strength to grip a weapon and stand between these islands and whatever comes to claim them, the world will not be the one to decide when we are finished."
