L0_1.il_grande_cerchio = L1_1
L1_1 = {}
L1_1.mode = "text"
L1_1.title = "The Code of the Sons"
L1_1.author = "Archive of the Great Circle"
L1_1.text = "A Son may enter the Circle. But the moment he crosses its boundary, he enters as a man. This is the first law, and no champion, Arbiter, or leader of the islands has the authority to change it. Within the Circle, a Son does not fly. He does not summon flames. He does not bend space. He calls upon none of the gifts granted by Decay. Anyone who needs his power to defeat a man proves only that he is a slave to what he possesses. And control is what separates a Son from a beast. For this reason, before every fight, the Seal of the Circle is activated. When the Seal answers, every gift falls silent. Only breath, blade, and will remain. Within the Circle, a Son bleeds like any other man. His bones can break. His heart can stop. And a man with no gift at all can bring him down before thousands of witnesses. It is precisely this possibility that makes the fight worthy. We do not worship the Sons. We do not fear them. We observe them. A Son capable of willingly surrendering his superiority to face a man on equal ground proves that he possesses something rarer than strength: discipline. If he fights with honor, he becomes an example. If he attempts to break the Seal, calls upon his gift, or uses Decay against an opponent, he becomes a warning. The fight is stopped, and his name is erased from the Archive of Champions. Remember, then, the oldest law of the Circle: there are no chosen ones here. There are no superior beings here. There are no monsters here. There are only men, stripped of everything they might hide behind, forced to show before all others what they have chosen to become."
