L1_1 = {}
L1_1.mode = "text"
L1_1.title = "Children of the Land"
L1_1.author = "Stables of the Mother Isle"
L1_1.text = "When the world filled with water, we lost cities, roads, fields, and almost everything we once believed indispensable. But we did not lose everything. The horses remained with us. At first, some considered them merely another means of survival. They were wrong. A horse is not transportation. It is a companion. It carries supplies to outposts when the roads become dangerous, drags the wounded away from attacks, travels with caravans, and carries warriors where boats cannot reach. For this reason, owning a horse is not a privilege, but a responsibility. No animal is left unattended. The stables are protected like stores of Eteris. Feed is grown even when the harvest is scarce, and their wounds are tended before many wounds suffered by men. Some consider such care excessive. Those people have never had to cross an island wounded, in darkness, with something behind them. An island that mistreats its horses soon discovers just how long its roads truly are. During the Tournaments of the Three Moons, champions still arrive on horseback. Not for spectacle. They do so to remember that before entering the Circle, they traveled paths, crossed forests, protected caravans, and faced creatures alongside the animal that carried them there. A horse is not earned merely with what a man possesses. A horse is earned through care. As long as we hear hooves running along the roads of the islands, we will know that there are still paths left to travel, men brave enough to cross them, and something in this world that has chosen to survive alongside us."
