L1_1.title = "The Building Code"
L1_1.author = "Council of the Three Lands"
L1_1.text = "It was decreed that no structure would be raised for vanity alone, and that every material would serve function before form. The height of a structure shall not exceed what its purpose requires. Rare wood belongs first to boats, bridges, and structures that keep communities connected, and only afterward to decoration. Forged metal belongs first to tools, defenses, and weapons. Volcanic stone shall not be consumed by walls built merely to display the wealth of an island. Every harbor shall be recognizable from the sea, but never needlessly bright. Every Arena shall be strong enough to contain the men who fight within it, but never so monumental that it consumes what could instead protect those living around it. Every home shall provide shelter before it provides prestige. To build is to transform a limited resource into something capable of enduring. For this reason, wasting material is not merely poor stewardship: it is taking safety away from someone who may need it tomorrow. Finally, remember what fishermen teach their children: anything that rises too high becomes visible even to whatever watches from the sea. No one knows whether this is truly so. The Code does not require us to find out."
