L1_1.title = "Beyond the Limit"
L1_1.author = "Log of a Lost Expedition"
L1_1.text = "I do not write for glory. I write so that someone may find these pages before they find what we found. Beyond the line of the currents, the sea changes. I know no other way to describe it. The water grows heavier against the hull, and the wind continues to blow without ever filling the sails. Even sounds seem more distant. For hours, we saw nothing. That was the deception. The silence convinced us that we had been afraid of something that did not exist. Then we saw the first one. It was not a fish. It was not a whale. I have no word for what it was. An enormous mass moved slowly through the water beneath us, and for a moment I had the absurd impression that it was not a creature moving through the sea, but the sea itself given flesh. More of them came. Some approached the vessels without touching them. They remained beneath us, followed our course, and then disappeared. They seemed to be watching us. On the third night, one of the expedition's ships vanished. It was not shattered. We heard no screams. Something surfaced beneath it, and when the water became still again, the ship simply no longer existed. We decided to turn back. That was when the great one came. The water trembled before we could even see its shadow. The other creatures vanished immediately. Not one remained near our boats. For a moment, we believed it had come for us. It passed beneath our hulls without touching them and continued toward the boundary of the currents. I recognized it. We all did. It was the Shadow we had spent years believing was preventing us from leaving the islands. But that night, it was not preventing us from getting out. It was preventing them from getting in. If this log ever reaches the islands, do not make our mistake. Not everything that keeps us trapped is necessarily our jailer. And not everything waiting outside wants the door to remain closed."
