L1_1.title = "Fragments of the Forbidden Isle"
L1_1.author = "Unknown Author"
L1_1.text = "The island does not appear on any official map. None of the Founders claim it, no banner has ever been raised upon it, and the oldest sailors change the subject whenever someone asks which current leads to its shores. And yet, the island exists. I have walked upon its soil. The structures that stand there resemble nothing built after the Flooding. They are too large, too deep, and in some places seem to continue directly into the rock itself. Time-worn carvings remain upon the walls. Many are illegible. Two words appear again and again: transformation and threshold. Another figure appears beside them. A man facing the sea. He does not fight. He does not flee. He seems to be waiting. In the deepest part of the island, we found a chamber. At its center stood something we initially mistook for a cauldron. It did not rest upon the stone. It was fused with it. Around it, we found layers of hardened ash and blue residue so concentrated that one of our men began trembling after merely touching it. It was Eteris, or something similar enough to frighten us. None of the islands could produce such a quantity in a single place. That night, the dreams began. Black water. A blue light in the depths. And a slow heartbeat that did not come from our own chests. By morning, two men wanted to stay. They could not explain why. We dragged them back to the boat. Later, in the records of the Founders, I found only a single mention of the island: \"Do not claim.\" Not \"useless.\" Not \"dangerous.\" Only \"do not claim.\" Now I believe I understand at least part of the reason. Some lands are abandoned because they hold no value. Others because they hold a value no one should yet know how to use."
