L1_1.title = "The Name Velario"
L1_1.author = "Archive of the First Voyages"
L1_1.text = "No one knows what the creature was called before the Flooding, or whether it ever had a name at all. The name Velario was given to it by men much later, when the first navigators began to understand that the great Shadow did not wander freely across the sea. It appeared almost always in the same place: where the currents changed and the known waters gave way to something no map could describe. The ancients called a great sheet of cloth stretched above something to shield it from the light and from what came from outside a velarium. In time, that word took on another meaning. Veil. Boundary. Something placed between two worlds. Sailors thus began calling the creature Velario, because wherever it appeared there seemed to be a line no man was meant to cross. Some claim the name means \"the one who conceals.\" Others prefer \"the one who separates.\" For generations, the Wardens interpreted the name as that of our jailer: the creature was the veil preventing mankind from seeing and reaching whatever exists beyond the sea. The Seekers of the Horizon preserve a more unsettling interpretation. Perhaps the veil does not exist to prevent us from looking out. Perhaps it exists to prevent whatever is outside from looking in. No Archive declares which interpretation is true. Only the name remains. Velario. The veil between what we know and what we were never meant to know."
